InetSocketAddress, and HttpServer.createContext registers a handler for a path prefix. In the handler, add
the Content-Type header to the exchange''s response headers before calling HttpExchange.sendResponseHeaders
with the status and the length. Files.probeContentType can return null, so keep a small map from extension
to type for html, css and js.', 'generated') on conflict (concept_id, language, framework) do update set body = excluded.body;
delete from resource where concept_id = (select id from concept where slug = 'file-watching') and url <> all(array['https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/inotify.7.html', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inotify', 'https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winbase/nf-winbase-readdirectorychangesw', 'https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/nio/file/WatchService.html']::text[]);
subdirectories, so register each one yourself, for example while walking the tree with Files.walkFileTree.
WatchService.take waits for the next batch of events, and WatchKey.reset must be called afterwards or the
key stops delivering. On some platforms the built-in implementation polls, so changes can arrive late.', 'generated') on conflict (concept_id, language, framework) do update set body = excluded.body;
